<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Environmental Product Declaration</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 {
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        th, td {
            padding: 8px;
            text-align: left;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
        }
        th {
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Environmental Product Declaration</h1>
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 40px;">for <span data-field="product_name">{{ product_name }}</span></p>

        <!-- Image Placeholder Area -->
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 50px;">
            <!-- Placeholder for product images -->
            <img src="placeholder_product_image.png" alt="Product Image" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 50px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Organisational framework</h2>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    <span data-field="company_name">{{ company_name }}</span> in <span data-field="location_country">{{ location_country }}</span> forms part of <span data-field="group_name">{{ group_name }}</span> segment. The company develops, manufactures and markets electrical machines and drives for <span data-field="group_focus">{{ group_focus }}</span> customers worldwide and is responsible for several key product groups, including variable-speed AC drives and drive systems for speed control of electric motors.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Product description</h2>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    <span data-field="group_description">{{ group_description }}</span> comprises the following product lines:
                </p>
                <ul style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_1">{{ product_line_1 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_2">{{ product_line_2 }}</span> power range: <span data-field="power_range_1">{{ power_range_1 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_3">{{ product_line_3 }}</span> power range: <span data-field="power_range_2">{{ power_range_2 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_4">{{ product_line_4 }}</span> power range: <span data-field="power_range_3">{{ power_range_3 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_5">{{ product_line_5 }}</span> power range: <span data-field="power_range_4">{{ power_range_4 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_6">{{ product_line_6 }}</span> power range: <span data-field="power_range_5">{{ power_range_5 }}</span></li>
                    <li><span data-field="product_line_7">{{ product_line_7 }}</span> power range: <span data-field="power_range_6">{{ power_range_6 }}</span></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Environmental management</h2>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    The <span data-field="standard_name">{{ standard_name }}</span> international environmental management standard has been implemented and the <span data-field="policy_name">{{ policy_name }}</span> has been certified since <span data-field="certification_year">{{ certification_year }}</span>. Life cycle assessment is applied continually to all product development.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Environmental product declaration</h2>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    This document applies to the <span data-field="product_model">{{ product_model }}</span> <span data-field="product_spec">{{ product_spec }}</span> which is a <span data-field="product_power">{{ product_power }}</span>, <span data-field="product_voltage">{{ product_voltage }}</span>, <span data-field="product_phase">{{ product_phase }}</span>.
                </p>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Material according to the table below is used for the product.
                </p>
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="width: 50%;">Type of material</th>
                            <th style="width: 25%; text-align: right;">kg / product</th>
                            <th style="width: 25%; text-align: right;">% kg</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Steel</td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_steel_kg">{{ material_steel_kg }}</span></td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_steel_pct">{{ material_steel_pct }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Copper</td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_copper_kg">{{ material_copper_kg }}</span></td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_copper_pct">{{ material_copper_pct }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Aluminium</td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_aluminium_kg">{{ material_aluminium_kg }}</span></td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_aluminium_pct">{{ material_aluminium_pct }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Plastics</td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_plastics_kg">{{ material_plastics_kg }}</span></td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_plastics_pct">{{ material_plastics_pct }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Cardboard (package)</td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_cardboard_kg">{{ material_cardboard_kg }}</span></td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_cardboard_pct">{{ material_cardboard_pct }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Other materials</td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_other_kg">{{ material_other_kg }}</span></td>
                            <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="material_other_pct">{{ material_other_pct }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Environmental performance</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            The data and calculations are in accordance with <span data-field="standard_reference_1">{{ standard_reference_1 }}</span> for Variable Speed Electric Drives, which specifies the following baselines for the LCA calculation.
        </p>

        <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Functional unit</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            The functional unit for the LCA is <span data-field="functional_unit_description">{{ functional_unit_description }}</span>.
        </p>

        <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px;">System boundaries</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            The life cycle assessment covers all environmental aspects for extraction and production of raw materials, manufacturing of main parts, assembly, transportation and use of the product, dismantling, fragmentation and disposal and recycling of scrap after end of life. It includes consumption of material and energy resources as well as emissions and waste generation.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            Calculations are based on an estimated lifetime of <span data-field="lifetime_years">{{ lifetime_years }}</span> when operating <span data-field="operating_hours">{{ operating_hours }}</span>. A finish mix of energy has been used for calculating energy consumption during manufacturing and an OECD mix of energy for calculating energy consumption during use and disposal.
        </p>

        <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px;">Allocation unit</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            The factor for allocation of common environmental aspects during manufacturing (such as manufacturing waste) is calculated as used working hours in relation to the total annual production volume.
        </p>

        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Resource utilisation</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width: 40%;">Use of non-renewable resources</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Manufacturing phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Usage phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Disposal phase</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Coal kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_coal_mfg">{{ resource_coal_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_coal_use">{{ resource_coal_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_coal_disp">{{ resource_coal_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Aluminium (Al) kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_al_mfg">{{ resource_al_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_al_use">{{ resource_al_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_al_disp">{{ resource_al_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Copper (Cu) kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_cu_mfg">{{ resource_cu_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_cu_use">{{ resource_cu_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_cu_disp">{{ resource_cu_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Iron (Fe) kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_fe_mfg">{{ resource_fe_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_fe_use">{{ resource_fe_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_fe_disp">{{ resource_fe_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Manganese (Mn) kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_mn_mfg">{{ resource_mn_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_mn_use">{{ resource_mn_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_mn_disp">{{ resource_mn_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Nickel (Ni) kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_ni_mfg">{{ resource_ni_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_ni_use">{{ resource_ni_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_ni_disp">{{ resource_ni_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Uranium (U) kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_u_mfg">{{ resource_u_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_u_use">{{ resource_u_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_u_disp">{{ resource_u_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Oil kg</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_oil_mfg">{{ resource_oil_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_oil_use">{{ resource_oil_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="resource_oil_disp">{{ resource_oil_disp }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Energy consumption and losses</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width: 30%;">Energy</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Manufacturing phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Usage phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Disposal phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 10%; text-align: right;">Total life cycle</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Electrical</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_elec_mfg">{{ energy_elec_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_elec_use">{{ energy_elec_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_elec_disp">{{ energy_elec_disp }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_elec_total">{{ energy_elec_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Heat</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_heat_mfg">{{ energy_heat_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_heat_use">{{ energy_heat_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_heat_disp">{{ energy_heat_disp }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="energy_heat_total">{{ energy_heat_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 20px;">
            The average finish electricity mix is defined as being <span data-field="mix_elec_pct_1">{{ mix_elec_pct_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_elec_pct_2">{{ mix_elec_pct_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_elec_pct_3">{{ mix_elec_pct_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_elec_pct_4">{{ mix_elec_pct_4 }}</span> and <span data-field="mix_elec_pct_5">{{ mix_elec_pct_5 }}</span>. The average OECD electrical energy is defined as being <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_1">{{ mix_oecd_pct_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_2">{{ mix_oecd_pct_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_3">{{ mix_oecd_pct_3 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_4">{{ mix_oecd_pct_4 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_5">{{ mix_oecd_pct_5 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_6">{{ mix_oecd_pct_6 }}</span>, <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_7">{{ mix_oecd_pct_7 }}</span> & <span data-field="mix_oecd_pct_8">{{ mix_oecd_pct_8 }}</span>. The resultant resource utilisation is shown in the table above.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">Waste</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width: 50%;">Waste</th>
                    <th style="width: 25%; text-align: right;">kg / kW</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Hazardous waste</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;">-</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>During manufacturing</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="waste_mfg_kg">{{ waste_mfg_kg }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>At disposal phase</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="waste_disp_kg">{{ waste_disp_kg }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Regular waste (to landfill)</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="waste_landfill_kg">{{ waste_landfill_kg }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>During manufacturing phase</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="waste_mfg_phase_kg">{{ waste_mfg_phase_kg }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>At disposal phase</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="waste_disp_phase_kg">{{ waste_disp_phase_kg }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">The classification data for emissions are as follows.</h2>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width: 40%;">Environmental effect</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Equivalent unit</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Manufacturing phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 20%; text-align: right;">Usage phase</th>
                    <th style="width: 10%; text-align: right;">Total life cycle</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Global warming potential GWP</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;">kg CO2 eq / kW</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="gwp_mfg">{{ gwp_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="gwp_use">{{ gwp_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="gwp_total">{{ gwp_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Acidification potential AP</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;">kg SO2 eq / kW</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="ap_mfg">{{ ap_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="ap_use">{{ ap_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="ap_total">{{ ap_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Eutrophication potential EUT</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;">kg PO4 eq / kW</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="eut_mfg">{{ eut_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="eut_use">{{ eut_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="eut_total">{{ eut_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Ozone depletion potential ODP</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;">kg CFC-11 eq / kW</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="odp_mfg">{{ odp_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="odp_use">{{ odp_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="odp_total">{{ odp_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Photochemical oxidants PCOP</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;">kg ethene / kW</td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="pcop_mfg">{{ pcop_mfg }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="pcop_use">{{ pcop_use }}</span></td>
                    <td style="text-align: right;"><span data-field="pcop_total">{{ pcop_total }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Additional qualifying factors</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            <span data-field="factor_description">{{ factor_description }}</span>
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            The main parts of the product can be recycled - some parts need to be fragmented to separate different types of material. A list of parts and components that can be fragmented and recycled can be obtained from the manufacturer. See references.
        </p>

        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Glossary</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Usage phase in relation to the total</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    It should be observed that the environmental impact during the usage phase is the most important. As an example, GWP for the usage phase is approximately <span data-field="usage_gwp_value">{{ usage_gwp_value }}</span> than GWP for the manufacturing phase.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Acidification, AP</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Acidification originates from the emissions of sulphur dioxide and oxides of nitrogen. These emissions react with water in the atmosphere to form acids which subsequently fall down to the earth in the form of rain or snow, or as dry deposition. Acidification potential translates the quantity of emission of a substance to a common measure to compare their contributions to the capacity to release hydrogen ions.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 20px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Eutrophication</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Nutrients (mainly nitrogen and phosphorus) from sewage outlets and fertilised agricultural land can cause eutrophication. Eutrophication potential translates the quantity of emission of a substance to a common measure expressed as the oxygen requirement for the degraded of dead biomass.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Global warming, GWP</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Global warming is the earth's atmosphere in particular water vapour and carbon dioxide have an ability to absorb infrared radiation. They do not prevent the earth's surface from heating up, but they trap some of the infrared radiation back into the atmosphere, causing an increase in the earth's temperature. Global Warming Potential, GWP100, translates the quantity of emission of gases to a common measure to compare their contributions to radiative balance over a 100 year period.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 20px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Ozone depletion, ODP</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Ozone depletion refers to the destruction of ozone layer in the stratosphere by certain chemicals, such as CFCs and halons released into the atmosphere. Ozone layer will increase the UV-radiation at ground level. Ozone depletion potential translates the quantity of emission of gases into a common measure to compare their contributions to the breakdown of the ozone layer.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Photochemical oxidants creation, PCOP</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
                    Photochemical oxidants are formed by the reaction of volatile organic compounds and nitrogen oxides in the presence of heat and sunlight. Photochemical oxidants are formed by the reaction of nitrogen oxides and volatile organic compounds in the presence of sunlight. PCOP translates the quantity of emission of gases into a common measure to compare their contributions - relative to ethene - to the formation of photochemical oxidants.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <h2 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">References</h2>
        <ul style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li><span data-field="ref_1">{{ ref_1 }}</span></li>
            <li><span data-field="ref_2">{{ ref_2 }}</span></li>
            <li><span data-field="ref_3">{{ ref_3 }}</span></li>
            <li><span data-field="ref_4">{{ ref_4 }}</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 30px;">
            The above mentioned documents are available upon request from <span data-field="contact_entity">{{ contact_entity }}</span>.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div style="position: fixed; bottom: 0; right: 60px; padding: 20px; font-family: 'DejaVu Serif', serif;">
        <img src="abb_logo.png" alt="ABB Logo" style="height: 50px;">
